.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "def __init__ ( self, \fBbus_stats\fP stats, queue\&.Queue raw_frame, queue\&.Queue processed_frame, \fBeds_parser\fP eds_map, str | None  export = \fCNone\fP, bool  sniffer = \fCFalse\fP)"

.PP
Initialize the processor thread\&. The constructor stores references to required helpers, initializes a stop event and logging, sets up CSV export if requested, and ensures statistics collection start time is set\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstats\fP Instance of \fBbus_stats\fP used to record statistics\&. 
.br
\fIraw_frame\fP \fCqueue\&.Queue\fP providing raw frames (dict) from the sniffer\&. 
.br
\fIprocessed_frame\fP \fCqueue\&.Queue\fP instance to push processed frames for display\&. 
.br
\fIeds_map\fP Instance of \fBeds_parser\fP from \fBeds_parser\&.py\fP used to resolve Object Dictionary names and PDO mappings\&. 
.br
\fIexport\fP \fCcsv\fP, \fCjson\fP: enable export of processed frames to a file\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "def _close_all_exports ( self)\fC [private]\fP"

.PP
Close every active processed-frame export\&. Callers must hold \fB_export_lock\fP\&. 
.SS "def _close_export ( self, str fmt)\fC [private]\fP"

.PP
Flush and close a single processed-frame export format\&. Finalizes the format's file (JSON array terminator, flush, fsync, close) then removes it from \fB_exports\fP\&. Callers must hold \fB_export_lock\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfmt\fP Export format to close\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "def _export_processed_frame_locked ( self, dict frame)\fC [private]\fP"

.PP
Write a processed frame to every active export format\&. Each active format (CSV, JSON) is written independently\&. Caller must hold \fB_export_lock\fP\&. 
.SS " dict _json_safe_processed_frame ( self, dict frame)\fC [private]\fP"

.PP
Create a processed frame for saving to JSON\&. 
.SS "def _open_export ( self, str fmt)\fC [private]\fP"

.PP
Open a processed-frame export for \fCfmt\fP and store its record\&. Opens the file/writer for \fCfmt\fP and writes any required header, registering a per-format record in \fB_exports\fP\&. \fCpcap\fP is accepted for symmetry with the sniffer but writes no processed file (only the raw sniffer stream is PCAP-capable); the record is still registered so both workers stay in sync\&. Formats are independent, so this never disturbs other active exports\&. Callers must hold \fB_export_lock\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfmt\fP Export format: 'csv', 'json', or 'pcap'\&. 
.RE
.PP

